            <div xml:id="d1016">

                <pb facs="0899" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/407a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Counselor of Embassy in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-30T13:00:00-05:00">November 30, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>384. Press report under Tokyo date line November 29 states that it is reported
                    from Tientsin that the Peace Maintenance Commission there has already reduced
                    tariffs on a long list of articles imported from Japan.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report promptly by naval radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
